# .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Revisions listed here are hidden from `git blame` output by passing
# `--ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs`.  GitHub also reads this
# file automatically (when the option is enabled in the repo settings).
#
# Use this for mass-formatting commits that are noise from the perspective
# of a normal blame history (e.g. the GTK_STOCK_ -> xsi-icon migration,
# the minizip -> libzip drop).  Add the most recent commit at the bottom,
# keep the file in chronological order, so the diff against the previous
# version of this file stays small.
#
# Example entry:
#   0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567  Short description of the change
